    FEATURE-004 Asset Management - AM-006 Asset Disposal Wizard Views
    ==================================================================

    Provides the form view and window action for the TransientModel
    ``account.asset.disposal.wizard``.  Supports three disposal methods
    in accordance with IAS 16 (Property, Plant and Equipment) derecognition
    requirements and US GAAP ASC 360-10-40 disposal rules:

      * ``sale``      - asset disposal with proceeds (cash or receivable
                        debit, asset credit, accumulated depreciation
                        debit, gain/loss recognition for any difference
                        between proceeds and net book value).
      * ``scrap``     - disposal with zero proceeds for obsolete or
                        damaged assets; remaining NBV (if any) recognized
                        as loss on disposal.
      * ``write_off`` - disposal for lost, stolen, or destroyed assets
                        with optional insurance recovery; remaining NBV
                        net of any recovery recognized as loss.

    Additional features supported by the wizard:
      * Automatic gain/loss calculation: Gain/Loss = Proceeds - NBV.
        Positive difference is credited to gain account; negative
        difference is debited to loss account.
      * Optional catch-up depreciation: when the disposal date is after
        the last posted depreciation entry, a prorated catch-up
        depreciation journal entry is generated automatically to bring
        accumulated depreciation current through the disposal date.
      * Partial disposal: disposing of a portion of an asset (e.g., 30
        of 100 units) with proportional acquisition cost, accumulated
        depreciation, and NBV calculations; the original asset record
        is updated to reflect the retained portion for continued
        depreciation.

    Called from the Asset form's header "Dispose" button via
    ``account.asset.action_dispose()``, which returns this action.  The
    action also binds to the ``account.asset`` model so it surfaces in
    the Action menu on asset records (contextual action).

    AAP Rule Compliance
    ===================
    * R-01 (Module independence) - No references to sibling CE modules
      (account_budget_management, account_deferred_revenue,
      account_payment_followup).  Only references this module's model
      ``account.asset.disposal.wizard`` (net-new TransientModel),
      ``account.asset`` (same module, net-new), and core Odoo models
      (``account.move``, ``account.account``, ``res.company``,
      ``res.currency``, ``base.group_multi_company``).
    * R-02 (No Enterprise deps) - No references to Enterprise modules
      in any field, action, or attribute.
    * R-05 (No core view modification) - This file defines NET-NEW views
      on a NET-NEW TransientModel; NO ``inherit_id`` attribute appears
      on any record.
    * R-07 (No sudo) - Not applicable; XML-only data file.
    * R-09 (Exact module folder name) - File lives in
      ``addons/account_asset_management/views/`` as required.

    Odoo 19.0 View Conventions Observed
    ===================================
    * ``invisible="expression"`` and ``readonly="expression"`` attributes
      (NOT ``attrs="..."``) per Odoo 17+ convention.
    * Boolean / comparison operators: ``and``, ``or``, ``not``, ``in``,
      ``not in``; comparisons use XML-escaped ``&gt;``, ``&lt;``, ``&amp;``.
    * 4-space indentation throughout.
    * ``<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>`` header.
-->
<odoo>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         WIZARD FORM VIEW
         ==================================================================
         The single form view for the ``account.asset.disposal.wizard``
         TransientModel.  Displays the target asset, disposal method and
         date, method-specific input groups (sale proceeds, partial
         disposal), gain/loss summary, documentation for audit trail,
         and post-state result links.

         Conditional visibility is driven by ``disposal_method``,
         ``is_partial``, ``catchup_depreciation_required``, ``state``,
         and ``gain_loss_amount`` so the wizard adapts to each disposal
         scenario without overwhelming the user with irrelevant fields.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="view_account_asset_disposal_wizard_form" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">account.asset.disposal.wizard.form</field>
        <field name="model">account.asset.disposal.wizard</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <form string="Dispose Asset">
                <!-- HEADER: state statusbar only. Action buttons live
                     in the <footer> block so Odoo suppresses the default
                     Save/Discard wizard buttons (Issue #5 fix). The
                     state field stays in the header so the statusbar
                     widget renders at the top of the form. -->
                <header>
                    <field name="state"
                           widget="statusbar"
                           statusbar_visible="draft,confirmed,posted"/>
                </header>
                <sheet>
                    <!-- CATCH-UP DEPRECIATION WARNING BANNER.
                         Per AM-006 Scenario 6 (disposal date validation
                         against depreciation schedule), when the disposal
                         date falls after the last posted depreciation
                         entry the system must compute prorated catch-up
                         depreciation through the disposal date.  This
                         alert informs the user that a separate catch-up
                         journal entry will be posted before the disposal
                         entry upon confirmation. -->
                    <div class="alert alert-warning" role="alert"
                         invisible="not catchup_depreciation_required">
                        <strong>Catch-up depreciation required:</strong>
                        Depreciation through the disposal date has not yet been
                        posted. A catch-up entry will be created automatically
                        when you post this disposal.
                    </div>

                    <!-- PRIMARY GROUP: Asset + Disposal metadata.
                         Two-column layout.  Left: asset and company context.
                         Right: disposal method (radio widget for clarity),
                         disposal date, and partial-disposal toggle. -->
                    <group>
                        <group string="Asset">
                            <field name="asset_id"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"
                                   options="{'no_create': True, 'no_open': False}"/>
                            <field name="company_id"
                                   groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
                            <field name="currency_id" invisible="1"/>
                        </group>
                        <group string="Disposal Details">
                            <field name="disposal_method"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"
                                   widget="radio"/>
                            <field name="disposal_date"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                            <field name="is_partial"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>

                    <!-- PARTIAL DISPOSAL GROUP (conditional).
                         Per AM-006 Scenario 5 (partial asset disposal),
                         visible only when ``is_partial`` is True.  The
                         user enters the disposed quantity; the system
                         computes the disposal_proportion (disposed /
                         total) which drives the proportional calculation
                         of acquisition cost, accumulated depreciation,
                         and NBV for the disposed portion. -->
                    <group string="Partial Disposal"
                           invisible="not is_partial">
                        <field name="disposed_quantity"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                        <field name="total_quantity"/>
                        <field name="disposal_proportion"
                               widget="percentage"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- SALE PROCEEDS GROUP (conditional).
                         Per AM-006 Scenario 1 (disposal by sale),
                         visible only when ``disposal_method`` is 'sale'.
                         Proceeds amount and destination account (cash or
                         accounts receivable) drive the proceeds debit
                         line of the disposal journal entry and the
                         gain/loss calculation.  ``no_create: True`` on
                         the account field prevents accidental inline
                         creation of account records. -->
                    <group string="Sale Proceeds"
                           invisible="disposal_method != 'sale'">
                        <field name="proceeds_amount"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"/>
                        <field name="proceeds_account_id"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               options="{'no_create': True}"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- GAIN / LOSS SUMMARY GROUP (always visible).
                         Per AM-006 Scenario 4 (automatic gain/loss
                         calculation), the system computes Gain/Loss =
                         Proceeds - NBV and displays the result before
                         disposal confirmation for user review.

                         Decorations on ``gain_loss_amount``:
                           success (green) when positive -> gain
                           danger  (red)   when negative -> loss
                         XML-escaped ``&gt;`` and ``&lt;`` operators are
                         required inside the double-quoted attribute.

                         Account selection is polarity-driven:
                           * ``gain_account_id`` shown only when the
                             computed amount is positive (visible when
                             amount is > 0, i.e. NOT <= 0).
                           * ``loss_account_id`` shown only when the
                             computed amount is negative (visible when
                             amount is < 0, i.e. NOT >= 0).
                           * When the amount is exactly zero, neither
                             account field is shown (no gain/loss entry
                             is posted in that case).

                         ``catchup_depreciation_amount`` is shown only
                         when catch-up depreciation is required so the
                         user can see the magnitude of the prorated
                         entry before confirmation. -->
                    <group string="Gain / Loss Summary">
                        <group>
                            <field name="net_book_value"/>
                            <field name="catchup_depreciation_required"/>
                            <field name="catchup_depreciation_amount"
                                   invisible="not catchup_depreciation_required"/>
                        </group>
                        <group>
                            <field name="gain_loss_amount"
                                   class="oe_inline"
                                   decoration-success="gain_loss_amount &gt; 0"
                                   decoration-danger="gain_loss_amount &lt; 0"/>
                            <field name="gain_account_id"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"
                                   invisible="gain_loss_amount &lt;= 0"/>
                            <field name="loss_account_id"
                                   readonly="state != 'draft'"
                                   options="{'no_create': True}"
                                   invisible="gain_loss_amount &gt;= 0"/>
                        </group>
                    </group>

                    <!-- DOCUMENTATION GROUP (required for audit trail).
                         Per AM-006 Scenarios 2 and 3 (scrapping and
                         write-off), the disposal reason is required
                         for audit trail completeness and the optional
                         documentation_ref captures external references
                         such as insurance claim numbers, police report
                         IDs, or sale invoice numbers. -->
                    <group string="Documentation">
                        <field name="disposal_reason"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               placeholder="Reason for disposal (required for audit trail)..."/>
                        <field name="documentation_ref"
                               readonly="state != 'draft'"
                               placeholder="External document reference (invoice #, work order, etc.)"/>
                    </group>

                    <!-- POSTED JOURNAL ENTRIES GROUP (post-state only).
                         After successful posting, displays read-only
                         links to the generated ``account.move`` records
                         for drill-through audit:
                           * ``move_id`` - the main disposal journal entry.
                           * ``catchup_depreciation_move_id`` - the
                             separate catch-up depreciation entry (only
                             visible if one was required and created).

                         ``no_create: True`` prevents accidental creation;
                         ``no_open: False`` keeps the "open record" icon
                         enabled for drill-through navigation. -->
                    <group string="Posted Journal Entries"
                           invisible="state != 'posted'">
                        <field name="move_id"
                               readonly="1"
                               options="{'no_create': True, 'no_open': False}"/>
                        <field name="catchup_depreciation_move_id"
                               readonly="1"
                               invisible="not catchup_depreciation_move_id"
                               options="{'no_create': True, 'no_open': False}"/>
                    </group>
                </sheet>
                <!-- FOOTER: action buttons. Placing them in <footer>
                     suppresses Odoo's default Save/Discard wizard
                     buttons that would otherwise appear at the bottom
                     of the modal (Issue #5 fix). Each button is gated
                     on the wizard state machine:
                         draft     -> Confirm / Cancel
                         confirmed -> Post Disposal / Cancel
                         posted    -> Close (terminal)
                         cancelled -> Close (terminal) -->
                <footer>
                    <button name="action_confirm"
                            string="Confirm"
                            type="object"
                            class="btn-primary"
                            invisible="state != 'draft'"
                            data-hotkey="q"/>
                    <button name="action_post"
                            string="Post Disposal"
                            type="object"
                            class="btn-primary"
                            invisible="state != 'confirmed'"
                            data-hotkey="q"/>
                    <button name="action_cancel"
                            string="Cancel"
                            type="object"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            invisible="state in ('posted', 'cancelled')"/>
                    <button special="cancel"
                            string="Close"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            invisible="state not in ('posted', 'cancelled')"
                            data-hotkey="z"/>
                    <button special="cancel"
                            string="Discard"
                            class="btn-secondary"
                            invisible="state in ('posted', 'cancelled')"
                            data-hotkey="z"/>
                </footer>
            </form>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         WINDOW ACTION
         ==================================================================
         Opens the disposal wizard as a modal dialog (``target="new"``).
         Two entry points:
             1. From the asset form's header "Dispose" button, where the
                Python method ``account.asset.action_dispose()`` returns
                this action with the asset_id pre-populated via context.
             2. From the Action menu on asset records (contextual action)
                via the ``binding_model_id`` reference.

         The model technical id ``model_account_asset`` is Odoo's
         canonical ``ir.model`` record id, auto-generated from the model
         name ``account.asset`` (dots replaced with underscores, prefixed
         with ``model_``).  This id is already referenced by the module's
         ``security/ir.model.access.csv``, confirming it exists after
         ``account.asset`` is registered at module load time.

         The explicit ``view_id`` reference ensures deterministic view
         resolution even if other form views on the wizard model are
         defined in future extensions.  ``binding_view_types="form"``
         restricts the contextual action to asset form views (not list
         views), matching the standard UX for per-record wizards.
         ================================================================== -->
    <record id="action_account_asset_disposal_wizard"
            model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Dispose Asset</field>
        <field name="res_model">account.asset.disposal.wizard</field>
        <field name="view_mode">form</field>
        <field name="view_id"
               ref="view_account_asset_disposal_wizard_form"/>
        <field name="target">new</field>
        <field name="binding_model_id" ref="model_account_asset"/>
        <field name="binding_view_types">form</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
